[node name="range_forest_background" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "MOUNTED EDITOR-OWNED RANGE SOURCE. This stable slot instantiates assets/source/range_forest_distinct_background.blend through its exported GLB. The northern blue body carries the accepted smaller plan form, an irregular exposed rock-to-skirt contact and a closed blue saddle connecting it to the inland blue range while staying clear of the highway tunnel portals. The source now holds 7,536 separate, selectable low-poly coastal rocks: 5,932 at the main northern massif, 704 at its twice-linear-sized western companion, 600 at the north-shore volcanic plug and 300 along its south-running connector shelf. Exact collision twins accompany each. The newest 3,200 rocks fill the main massif's formerly blank front beach band with overlapping talus dense at the massif toe and thinning into scattered waterward stones; the earlier 2,480 complete the other visible beach runs. Their authored exclusion bands preserve the north-coast highway and north town. The plug retains its accepted form, subtly off-centre crown and widened south-running sand shelf with a vertically lowered inland reveal; the full-range Option A recovery remains open. Edit the Blender source, not this wrapper or the GLB. The city, bridge, roads, cameras and protected anchors remain outside range edits."

